<h2 id="how">How to reach us</h2>
<p>The easiest way to get in touch is through the project's public issue tracker on GitHub. It keeps questions, bug reports and ideas in one place where they can be answered and where other people with the same question can find the answer.</p>
<p><a class="cta" href="https://github.com/speakercleanerapp/speakercleanerapp.github.io/issues">Open the issue tracker</a></p>
<p>To create a new issue you need a free GitHub account. Choose <strong>New issue</strong>, give it a short title and describe what you need.</p>

<h2 id="bugs">Reporting a problem with the tool</h2>
<p>If a tone does not play, the timer behaves oddly or a page looks broken, please include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Your device model, for example the phone brand and model name.</li>
<li>Your browser and its version, such as Safari on iOS 18 or Chrome on Android 15.</li>
<li>Which mode and speaker setting you used.</li>
<li>What you expected to happen and what happened instead.</li>
</ul>
<p>Please do not post personal information such as phone numbers or addresses in an issue, because issues are public.</p>

<h2 id="ideas">Suggestions and corrections</h2>
<p>Ideas for new modes, clearer instructions or translations are welcome. If you spot an error in a guide, open an issue with the page address and the sentence you think should change.</p>

<h2 id="repair">Repair questions</h2>
<p>We cannot diagnose individual devices or arrange repairs. If your speaker is still distorted after cleaning, contact your phone's manufacturer or a qualified repair shop.</p>
